1. Project Overview 

The Home SIEM & Detection Lab is a hands on cybersecurity project designed to simulate a small enterprise security monitoring environment within an isolated virtual lab. 

The project will involve deploying a Security Information and Event Management (SIEM) platform, configuring a Windows endpoint for enhanced security telemetry, collecting and analyzing logs, developing security detections, and investigating controlled security events. 

The primary SIEM platform will be Wazuh, hosted on an Ubuntu Server virtual machine. A Windows 11 virtual machine will act as the monitored endpoint and will use Sysmon and the Wazuh Agent to generate and forward detailed security telemetry. 

The project will progress from infrastructure deployment to security monitoring, detection engineering, investigation, and professional documentation. 

The purpose is not simply to install and use a SIEM, but to develop practical understanding of how security analysts collect telemetry, identify suspicious behavior, investigate alerts, create detections, and document security incidents. 

 

