18. Ethical Considerations 

This project will be conducted exclusively within an authorized laboratory environment. 

All systems used for testing will either be owned by me or explicitly authorized for security testing. 

The project will follow these principles: 

Authorization 

No external system, organization, network, account, or application will be tested without explicit authorization. 

Isolation 

Security simulations will be performed inside the controlled laboratory environment. 

Data Protection 

Real personal, organizational, authentication, or confidential information will not intentionally be collected. 

Safe Testing 

Testing will avoid destructive actions and unnecessary disruption to systems. 

Responsible Disclosure 

If a genuine vulnerability is discovered outside the intentionally vulnerable lab environment, it will not be exploited beyond what is necessary to validate the finding and will be handled according to an appropriate responsible-disclosure process. 

Documentation 

Security testing activities will be documented so that their purpose, scope, and authorization are clear. 

